{
  "name": "Screen customers against sanctions lists with ComplyAdvantage and Claude",
  "flow": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "module": "util:SetVariables",
      "version": 1,
      "parameters": null,
      "mapper": {
        "scope": "roundtrip",
        "variables": [
          {
            "name": "config_your_name",
            "value": "Your name — signs every outgoing message"
          },
          {
            "name": "config_your_email",
            "value": "you@example.com"
          },
          {
            "name": "config_your_company",
            "value": "Your company or brokerage"
          },
          {
            "name": "config_timezone",
            "value": "Europe/London"
          },
          {
            "name": "config_quiet_hours_start",
            "value": "21"
          },
          {
            "name": "config_quiet_hours_end",
            "value": "8"
          },
          {
            "name": "config_approval_mode",
            "value": "true"
          },
          {
            "name": "config_approver",
            "value": "#approvals — a Slack channel, or an email address"
          },
          {
            "name": "config_test_mode",
            "value": "true"
          },
          {
            "name": "config_schedule",
            "value": "scenario schedule: Onboarding event + daily screening + transaction event"
          }
        ]
      },
      "metadata": {
        "designer": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 0,
          "name": "Config (edit me)"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "module": "http:MakeRequest",
      "version": 4,
      "parameters": {
        "authenticationType": "apiKey"
      },
      "mapper": {
        "url": "https://api.complyadvantage.com/searches",
        "method": "post",
        "headers": [],
        "queryParameters": [],
        "parseResponse": true,
        "stopOnHttpError": true,
        "timeout": "",
        "allowRedirects": true,
        "shareCookies": false,
        "requestCompressedContent": true,
        "contentType": "json",
        "inputMethod": "jsonString",
        "jsonStringBodyContent": "{\n  \"search_term\": \"{{ $json.full_name }}\",\n  \"client_ref\": \"{{ $json.customer_id }}\",\n  \"fuzziness\": 0.6,\n  \"filters\": {\n    \"types\": [\n      \"sanction\",\n      \"pep\",\n      \"adverse-media\"\n    ]\n  }\n}"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "designer": {
          "x": 300,
          "y": 0,
          "name": "ComplyAdvantage API: Screen the customer"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "module": "anthropic-claude:createAMessage",
      "version": 1,
      "parameters": {},
      "mapper": {
        "model": "claude-sonnet-5",
        "system": "You are the \"Pre-assess matches\" step of the KYC/AML Monitoring Workflow workflow run by Agentmelt.\nTask: For each hit the agent compares the customer profile to the list entry — dates, locations, identifiers, context — and drafts an assessment: likely true match, likely false positive, or needs more information, with the reasoning.\n\nRules:\n- No case is closed without an analyst's recorded decision; the agent drafts, never decides.\n- Sanctions matches always reach a senior analyst regardless of the draft assessment.\n- Every decision is logged in a tamper-evident store with actor, rationale and timestamp.\n- Rules and thresholds are versioned; changes require compliance-officer approval and are logged.\n- Answer only from the data provided in the input. If something is missing, say so in the output instead of guessing.\n- If this step produces a message or a document, put the full text in `draft` (and a `subject` if it is an email); put a one-line summary in `summary`.\n- Set `needs_human` true whenever you are unsure, the input is unusual, or a rule above applies; a person will look at it.\n- Return valid JSON matching the output schema; no prose outside the JSON.\n\nReply with a single JSON object and nothing else: the fields the task needs, plus \"needs_human\" (true when unsure), \"confidence\" (0–1) and \"summary\" (one line).",
        "messages": [
          {
            "role": "user",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Pre-assess matches.\n\nItem (map the fields your source provides here):\n{{2.text}}{{2.body}}{{2.message}}{{2.subject}}{{2.email}}{{2.name}}{{2.data}}"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "max_tokens": "2000",
        "temperature": "0.2",
        "metadata": {}
      },
      "metadata": {
        "designer": {
          "x": 600,
          "y": 0,
          "name": "Claude: Pre-assess matches"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "module": "json:ParseJSON",
      "version": 1,
      "parameters": {},
      "mapper": {
        "json": "{{3.textResponse}}"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "designer": {
          "x": 900,
          "y": 0,
          "name": "Parse Claude's JSON: Pre-assess matches"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "module": "builtin:BasicRouter",
      "version": 1,
      "parameters": null,
      "mapper": null,
      "metadata": {
        "designer": {
          "x": 1200,
          "y": 0,
          "name": "Gate: Pre-assess matches"
        }
      },
      "routes": [
        {
          "flow": [
            {
              "id": 13,
              "module": "builtin:ThrowWarning",
              "version": 1,
              "parameters": {},
              "mapper": {
                "message": "Parked for a person — Pre-assess matches: {{4.summary}}"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "designer": {
                  "x": 1500,
                  "y": 0,
                  "name": "Needs a person: Pre-assess matches"
                }
              },
              "filter": {
                "name": "Needs a person?",
                "conditions": [
                  [
                    {
                      "a": "{{4.needs_human}}",
                      "b": "true",
                      "o": "boolean:equal"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "flow": [
            {
              "id": 5,
              "module": "util:SetVariables",
              "version": 1,
              "parameters": null,
              "mapper": {
                "scope": "roundtrip",
                "variables": [
                  {
                    "name": "result",
                    "value": ""
                  }
                ]
              },
              "metadata": {
                "designer": {
                  "x": 1500,
                  "y": 150,
                  "name": "Evaluate transactions (port the rule here)"
                }
              },
              "filter": {
                "name": "Continue",
                "conditions": [
                  [
                    {
                      "a": "{{4.needs_human}}",
                      "b": "true",
                      "o": "boolean:notequal"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": 6,
              "module": "util:SetVariables",
              "version": 1,
              "parameters": null,
              "mapper": {
                "scope": "roundtrip",
                "variables": [
                  {
                    "name": "result",
                    "value": ""
                  }
                ]
              },
              "metadata": {
                "designer": {
                  "x": 1800,
                  "y": 150,
                  "name": "Build the case (port the rule here)"
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "id": 7,
              "module": "slack:CreateMessage",
              "version": 4,
              "parameters": {},
              "mapper": {
                "channelType": "public",
                "channel": "{{1.config_approver}}",
                "text": "Approve? {{4.summary}}\n\nReply in the thread with APPROVE or REJECT. With config_approval_mode = true nothing is written until the item is re-run with approved = true.",
                "parseText": false,
                "mrkdwn": true
              },
              "metadata": {
                "designer": {
                  "x": 2100,
                  "y": 150,
                  "name": "Slack approval: Route to the analyst"
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "id": 12,
              "module": "builtin:BasicRouter",
              "version": 1,
              "parameters": null,
              "mapper": null,
              "metadata": {
                "designer": {
                  "x": 2400,
                  "y": 150,
                  "name": "Approval gate: Route to the analyst"
                }
              },
              "routes": [
                {
                  "flow": [
                    {
                      "id": 11,
                      "module": "builtin:ThrowWarning",
                      "version": 1,
                      "parameters": {},
                      "mapper": {
                        "message": "Approval requested. Re-run the item with approved = true (or set config_approval_mode = false) to write it back."
                      },
                      "metadata": {
                        "designer": {
                          "x": 2700,
                          "y": 150,
                          "name": "Waiting for approval: Route to the analyst"
                        }
                      },
                      "filter": {
                        "name": "Approval mode on",
                        "conditions": [
                          [
                            {
                              "a": "{{1.config_approval_mode}}",
                              "b": "true",
                              "o": "text:equal"
                            }
                          ]
                        ]
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "flow": [
                    {
                      "id": 8,
                      "module": "postgres:Query",
                      "version": 2,
                      "parameters": {
                        "continueWhenNoRes": false,
                        "isToManageDataInSharedTransaction": true
                      },
                      "mapper": {
                        "query": "SELECT 1; -- replace with your query"
                      },
                      "metadata": {
                        "designer": {
                          "x": 2700,
                          "y": 300,
                          "name": "Postgres: Record the decision"
                        }
                      },
                      "filter": {
                        "name": "Approved or approval mode off",
                        "conditions": [
                          [
                            {
                              "a": "{{1.config_approval_mode}}",
                              "b": "false",
                              "o": "text:equal"
                            }
                          ],
                          [
                            {
                              "a": "{{1.approved}}",
                              "b": "true",
                              "o": "boolean:equal"
                            }
                          ]
                        ]
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "id": 9,
                      "module": "util:SetVariables",
                      "version": 1,
                      "parameters": null,
                      "mapper": {
                        "scope": "roundtrip",
                        "variables": [
                          {
                            "name": "run_at",
                            "value": "{{now}}"
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      "metadata": {
                        "designer": {
                          "x": 3000,
                          "y": 300,
                          "name": "Continuous re-screening (runs on the scenario schedule)"
                        }
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "id": 10,
                      "module": "google-docs:createADocument",
                      "version": 1,
                      "parameters": {},
                      "mapper": {
                        "name": "{{4.subject}}",
                        "content": "{{4.draft}}",
                        "destination": "drive",
                        "folderId": ""
                      },
                      "metadata": {
                        "designer": {
                          "x": 3300,
                          "y": 300,
                          "name": "Google Docs: Regulatory reporting"
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "metadata": {
    "instant": false,
    "version": 1,
    "scenario": {
      "roundtrips": 1,
      "maxErrors": 3,
      "autoCommit": true,
      "autoCommitTriggerLast": true,
      "sequential": false,
      "slots": null,
      "confidential": false,
      "dataloss": false,
      "dlq": false,
      "freshVariables": false
    },
    "designer": {
      "orphans": []
    },
    "notes": [
      {
        "moduleIds": [
          1
        ],
        "content": "## Screen customers against sanctions lists with ComplyAdvantage and Claude\n\nCompliance teams at fintechs and payment companies that screen and re-screen by hand.\n\n### How it works\nTrigger: New customers screened at onboarding; the full book re-screened daily against list updates; transaction events evaluated in near real time.\n1. Screen the customer\n2. Pre-assess matches\n3. Evaluate transactions\n4. Build the case\n5. Route to the analyst\n6. Record the decision\n7. Continuous re-screening\n8. Regulatory reporting\nEvery AI step is followed by a \"Needs a person?\" gate that parks low-confidence items; the write-back waits for an approval.\n\n### Setup\n1. Open \"Config (edit me)\" and fill in the fields (names, approver, quiet hours, thresholds).\n2. Add credentials: Anthropic, plus ComplyAdvantage / Dow Jones / OpenSanctions, Postgres.\n3. Run once with test_mode on, read the output, then switch the trigger on.\n\n### Customization tips\nSet the screening sources and the match thresholds in the Config node; this template assumes self-hosted n8n and a Postgres audit table.\nGuardrail to keep: No case is closed without an analyst's recorded decision; the agent drafts, never decides.\n\nFull blueprint: https://agentmelt.com/workflows/kyc-aml-monitoring/",
        "isFilterNote": false,
        "metadata": {
          "color": "#F5D451"
        }
      }
    ],
    "zone": "eu1.make.com"
  }
}